Hi William,
I guess I’m not super surprised by this given that you only have 11 treatment schools.  So I think it’s probably just very sensitive to the specific variables, and while your intuition is right I think there’s probably just some strange things happening because of your tiny treatment group sample size.

So in this example seems like you should match on school size since then you get better balance on that and on the other covariates.

Liz


